# Cursor Rules

## Git
- Never add "Co-authored-by: Cursor" or any AI attribution to git commits
- Write clean, descriptive commit messages in imperative mood (e.g. "Add dashboard screen")
- Stage only relevant files, never commit .env or secrets

## Figma → Vue (UI from mockups)

### Before writing markup
- Call Figma MCP (`get_design_context` or `get_metadata`) for the **exact frame** the user linked (`node-id`), not the whole file.
- Read the design **structure first**: outer padding, inner content width, gaps between sections, fixed field heights, border radius.
- Distinguish **final screens** vs wireframes — only implement what the user marked as final.
- Check `api-1.json` / OpenAPI before adding form fields (e.g. do not send `description` if the endpoint only accepts `name`).

### Tailwind must actually apply (critical)
- **Never** put Tailwind class strings only in `<script>` variables (e.g. `const fieldClass = 'bg-neutral-800 ...'`). The compiler will not generate CSS for them → inputs stay browser-default.
- **Do** use one of:
  - literal `class="..."` on elements in `<template>`, or
  - scoped `<style>` with `@reference '@/assets/styles/main.css'` and `@apply ...` (project pattern, same as `field-input` / `BaseInput.vue`).
- Reuse existing tokens when they match: `.field-input`, `btn-base`, CSS variables from `variables.css`.

### Sizes & proportions (no “convenient” substitutes)
- Never hardcode arbitrary pixels: no `w-[539px]`, `gap-[81px]`, `h-[52px]`.
- **Do** map each Figma value to the **nearest standard Tailwind token** and prefer that token consistently:
  - Example: content 539px + horizontal padding 72px each → card ≈ 683px → `max-w-2xl` + `px-18`, not `max-w-xl`.
  - Gaps: 44px → `gap-11`, 19px → `gap-5`, 81px → `gap-20`, 72px → `px-18`, 52px field → `h-13`, 133px textarea → `h-33`.
- “No hardcode” ≠ “pick any Tailwind class” — wrong token breaks layout as much as wrong pixels.
- For **fixed heights** from Figma, use `h-*` / `min-h-*`, not only `py-*` (padding alone will not match frame height).
- Mirror Figma **nested groups** in flex layout: separate `gap-*` for header→fields vs fields→button; do not collapse unrelated spacings into one parent gap.

### Layout & components
- Center modals with `fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center`; card uses `w-full max-w-* shrink-0 box-border`.
- Use `flex`, `items-center`, `justify-between`, `gap-*`; avoid inline styles.
- Do not import libraries (e.g. `motion`, UI kits) unless they already exist in `package.json`.
- Reuse project components (`BaseInput`, `BaseButton`) when behavior matches; custom `@apply` blocks only when the mockup diverges.

### Workflow per user request
- User provides: Figma link with `node-id`, target `.vue` file, task (layout / API / both), final vs wireframe.
- Implement **one screen or component** per iteration; confirm proportions against Figma screenshot before moving on.

## General Code Style
- Reuse existing components from the project before creating new ones
- Follow the existing folder structure and naming conventions
- Use TypeScript types, never use `any`
- Keep components small and single-responsibility

## API / Backend Integration
- Read OpenAPI/Swagger docs before writing any fetch logic
- Generate TypeScript types from the schema
- Follow the existing pattern for API calls in the project (axios/fetch/react-query)
- Never hardcode API URLs, use environment variables
- Handle loading and error states for every request